## Doc-path contract

`docs/SITEMAP.md` is the canonical doc-path contract. **Read it before creating any document.**
Every doc goes at the path SITEMAP gives it; no asset invents a path or a new top-level
directory. Four tiers, by lifetime:

| Lifetime | Path |
|---|---|
| Whole project | `docs/global/` |
| One milestone | `docs/milestones/<M>/` |
| One phase | `docs/milestones/<M>/phases/<NN>-<slug>/` |
| Machine state | `docs/state/` |

Repo root holds ecosystem files only — `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `LICENSE`,
`VERSION`, `CLAUDE.md`. Tool state stays under `.claude/`. Nothing else lives at the root.

## Project Constraints

Durable constraints that must hold on every turn — environment gotchas, tooling pins, standing
decisions. Loaded every session, so keep it a curated list, not a running log: one line each,
deleted when it stops being true. Narrative belongs in the docs it came from.

